# Extension version bump

Whenever you change any file under `extension/`, increment `extension/manifest.json` `"version"` in the same change.

Chrome parses each dotted part as an **integer**, so `1.01` becomes `1.1` and triggers a warning. Never use leading zeros.

- Use three-part versions: `1.1.1` → `1.1.2` → `1.1.3` (add 1 to the last number each update).
- The next version must be greater than the currently installed one (missing parts count as 0, so `1.1` == `1.1.0`).
- Do this even for small fixes. Do not leave the version unchanged after an extension edit.
- The popup and overlay read the version from the manifest; do not hardcode it elsewhere.
